@startuml uc-pat-01-comm-alt-a2
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8

title UC-PAT-01: Manage My Appointments (C5 v1.1.0)\nCommunication Diagram - Alternative Flow A2: Request Rescheduling (at step 7)

actor ":Patient" as pat
boundary ":MyAppointmentsUI" as ui
control ":PatientAppointmentController" as ctrl
control ":PatientAppointmentService" as srv
control ":AccessControlService (C1)" as c1
entity ":Booking" as booking
control ":AppointmentRules" as rules
entity ":RescheduleRequest" as req
control ":AuditService (C1)" as audit

pat -- ui : 1: chooseRequestRescheduling()\n2: enterReasonAndPreferredDates(reason, preferredDates) >\n< 7: displayRequestStatus(PENDING_REVIEW)

ui -- ctrl : 3: POST my-appointments/{bookingId}/reschedule-requests >\n< 6: HTTP 201 (RescheduleRequestStatusDTO)

ctrl -- srv : 4: requestRescheduling(PatientRescheduleRequestDTO) >\n< 5: RescheduleRequestStatusDTO

srv -- c1 : 4.1: canManageOwnAppointments(actorId, role) >

srv -- booking : 4.2: isOwnedBy(actorId) >

srv -- req : 4.5: findPending(bookingId) -> [none]\n4.6: create(bookingId, reason, preferredDates, PENDING_REVIEW) >

srv -- rules : 4.3: invalidRescheduleFields(request, today) -> [none]\n4.4: checkReschedule(booking, now) -> [active] >

srv -- audit : 4.7: recordEvent(APPOINTMENT_RESCHEDULE_REQUESTED) >

note bottom of booking
  The appointment is NOT changed (status, slot and version stay),
  so no BookingChangedEvent is published.
  Admissions Staff process the request in UC-AAD-05
  (ACCEPTED -> AAD-05 reschedule, or REJECTED).
  The patient sees the request status in the details (step 6).
end note
@enduml
